The legal texts come from the Assembleia da República de Moçambique:

  Constituição da República (2004), https://www.parlamento.mz/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Constituicao-da-Republica.pdf
  Legislação Básica (Secretariado-Geral da Assembleia da República, 2022),
  https://www.parlamento.mz/wp-content/uploads/2022/08/Legislacao_Basica.pdf
  both retrieved 2026-10-28.

They are official legislative texts. The Assembleia da República's site states no licence or terms for them. This
repository is private; whether and how it may be published is the owner's decision.

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per article, one paragraph per line;
spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; page numbers, running footers, title, chapter and section headings and
the closing approval and signature formula were left out; and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to
the laws that made each change. The wording of the law was not changed. The Assembleia da República does not endorse
this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
